From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: libipa: add a camera sensor helper for the S5K5E3YX

The Samsung Galaxy A3 (2015) front camera is an S5K5E3YX, which has no
helper, so the software ISP logs

  IPASoft: Failed to create camera sensor helper for s5k5e3

and falls back to treating the raw V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN code as a gain
multiplier. AEGC then converges on wildly wrong gains - the control's
minimum is 32, which the fallback reads as 32x rather than 1x.

The sensor uses the SMIA/MIPI analogue gain encoding, where the code is the
gain in 1/32 steps, so 0x0020 is unity. That matches the kernel driver,
whose control runs from 32 to 512 - 1x to 16x - with 32 as its default.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -780,6 +780,22 @@
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov5647", CameraSensorHelperOv5647)
 
+class CameraSensorHelperS5k5e3 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperS5k5e3()
+	{
+		/*
+		 * The gain registers (0x0204/0x0205) hold the SMIA analogue
+		 * gain code, which is the gain in 1/32 steps - 0x0020 is unity.
+		 * The sensor applies its own black level correction, so no
+		 * blackLevel_ is needed.
+		 */
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 32 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("s5k5e3", CameraSensorHelperS5k5e3)
+
 class CameraSensorHelperOv5648 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
 public:
